    "description": "The Signature Hybrid is Brooklyn Bedding's best-known mattress, and its main appeal is choice. It comes in soft, medium and firm, and Brooklyn Bedding itself recommends soft for side sleepers, medium for combination sleepers and firm for back and stomach sleepers. The current version stands 13.25 inches tall, or 14 inches with the optional Cloud Pillow Top. Under several foam layers sits an 8-inch core of up to 760 encased coils, according to the maker. RTINGS reports that the coils use different gauges: thicker 13-gauge coils at the head, foot and lumbar area, 14-gauge elsewhere and 15-gauge along the edges. In its evaluation, RTINGS rated pressure relief for side sleepers highest for heavier bodies, then average, and lower for light sleepers, who may not sink far enough. That makes it a strong match for heavier side sleepers, who should consider the soft or medium feel depending on how deep a cushion they want. The drawbacks: RTINGS describes most of the foam as low-density and expects it to soften sooner, and reviewers say it is not cool enough for hot sleepers. Brooklyn's own site lists a 365-night trial and limited lifetime warranty; one Amazon listing states a 10-year warranty, so check before buying."
