    "description": "The Leesa Original Hybrid adds a layer of pocketed springs to Leesa's original foam design, and the result is a balanced, responsive mattress that suits people who move around. It is 11 inches tall. Reviewers describe the build as roughly 1 inch of memory foam and 1.5 inches of polyfoam over 8 inches of individually pocketed coils, on a thin high-density foam base. That is less comfort foam than the Helix or Brooklyn carry, which is the point: you get enough cushioning for the shoulder and hip without sinking so deep that turning over becomes work. Reviewers place the feel between medium and medium-firm, with scores from 6 to 6.5 on 10-point scales, and one describes it as slightly softer than average. Pressure relief was above average for most testers in one review. The coils add bounce and let air circulate, so it should sleep cooler than an all-foam bed. For a strict side sleeper under about 130 pounds it may feel too firm, but for a combination sleeper in the average weight range it is a sensible middle ground. Sources disagree on the trial, citing 100 or 120 nights, and on the warranty; the Amazon listing states 10 years. Check the listing for current terms."
  },
  {
    "id": "nectar-classic-12",
    "name": "Nectar Classic 12\" Memory Foam Mattress",
