    "bottomLine": "The Nectar Classic is the value memory foam choice for average-weight side sleepers who want a supportive, slightly firmer bed and a full year to decide.",
    "description": "The Nectar Classic is a 12-inch all-foam mattress, and Nectar's strongest selling points are its terms: a 365-night trial and what it calls a Forever Warranty. That year-long trial matters more for side sleepers than most people realize, because it takes weeks for your body to adjust to a new surface and for the foam to break in. Nectar rates the feel at 6.5 out of 10, or medium-firm. Reviewers do not fully agree: Sleep Foundation lists it as a 6, Tom's Guide placed it nearer 7.5 in its testing, and one Amazon listing describes it as firm. Read that as a supportive memory foam bed rather than a plush one. For an average-weight side sleeper who also spends time on the back, that firmer support keeps the waist from sagging, while the memory foam top still molds to the shoulder and hip. Lighter strict side sleepers may find it too firm and should look at the Purple Restore Soft or the TEMPUR-Cloud instead, or plan on a topper. Reviewers also note that the slow-moving memory foam makes switching positions harder. Nectar sells a Classic Hybrid too, which is a different bed with coils; this pick is the all-foam model."
