    ],
    "cons": [
      "Reviewers say edge support is below average",
      "Zinus sells several similar Green Tea lines with different feels, which is confusing",
      "Reviewers report no Zinus sleep trial on the 12-inch model bought through Amazon"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The Zinus Green Tea is the budget pick for a lighter side sleeper or a guest room, as long as you accept weaker edges and simpler foam.",
    "description": "Zinus's Green Tea memory foam mattress is one of the best-known budget beds on Amazon, and the 12-inch version is the one to pick for side sleeping because it carries more comfort foam than the thinner sizes. The foam is infused with green tea and charcoal, which Zinus says keeps it fresh, and the maker lists it as CertiPUR-US certified and fiberglass free. The Queen listing gives a 500-pound weight limit. Firmness is where it gets confusing. Zinus sells several 12-inch Green Tea lines, including Essential and Cooling versions, and different listings describe the feel as medium, medium-firm or soft. Reviewers are split too: Sleep Foundation calls the line medium soft and Sleepopolis puts it around 5 out of 10, saying it gives strict side sleepers plenty of pressure relief at the hips and shoulders. Edge support is below average, which is typical of soft budget foam. It is a sensible bed for a lighter side sleeper, a teenager's room or a guest room. Heavier side sleepers should spend more on a hybrid. Tom's Guide reports that the 12-inch model sold on Amazon comes with a 10-year warranty but no Zinus sleep trial, so returns fall under the seller's policy. Check the exact listing before buying."
