          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The one rule that matters</h3>

          <p>
            Body weight decides firmness, and firmness decides everything else. A 120-pound side sleeper on a medium-firm bed barely sinks, so the shoulder takes the load. A 260-pound side sleeper on a soft bed sinks too far at the hips. Match the feel to your weight first, then choose foam or coils.
          </p>

          <p>
            Shopping for other sleep positions too? Our <a href="/best-mattress/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold no-underline hover:underline">guide to the top rated mattresses</a> covers back and stomach sleepers. This page stays on side sleeping, including hip pain and back pain.
          </p>
