        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best mattress for side sleepers?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most side sleepers, a medium hybrid with a thick comfort layer and zoned support works best. Our top pick is the Helix Midnight Luxe, which Helix designed around side sleepers. Lighter side sleepers may prefer something softer, such as the Purple Restore Soft, while heavier side sleepers should look at a sturdier hybrid like the Brooklyn Signature.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should side sleepers get a soft or firm mattress?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Most side sleepers do best on a soft to medium mattress, not a firm one. The shoulder and hip need to sink in so the spine stays straight. Body weight shifts the answer: under about 130 pounds, go soft to medium-soft; between 130 and 230, medium; above 230, medium to medium-firm with coil support.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best mattress for side sleepers with hip pain?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Look for a soft or medium mattress with a thick, pressure-relieving top layer and enough support underneath to keep the pelvis level. The Purple Restore Soft and Helix Midnight Luxe both fit. A pillow between the knees also helps keep the hips stacked. Persistent hip pain should be checked by a doctor or physical therapist.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best mattress for side sleepers with back pain?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A medium mattress with zoned or firmer lumbar support suits side sleepers with back pain, because it cushions the shoulder while keeping the waist from sagging. The Helix Midnight Luxe uses firmer coils under the lower back. If pain is persistent, runs down a leg or comes with numbness, see a doctor or physical therapist.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is memory foam or hybrid better for side sleepers?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Both work. Memory foam gives the deepest contouring and suits lighter side sleepers who like a hugging feel and do not move much. Hybrids add coil support and bounce, so they suit heavier side sleepers, combination sleepers and hot sleepers better. Hybrids generally cost more, which is why most budget picks are foam.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Why does my shoulder hurt when I sleep on my side?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Often the mattress is too firm, so the shoulder cannot sink and takes too much of your weight. A pillow that is too low can add to the strain. A softer mattress or topper and a higher pillow may help. Shoulder pain that lasts, or comes with weakness, should be assessed by a doctor or physical therapist.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a mattress topper make a firm mattress better for side sleeping?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes, if the mattress is otherwise in good shape. A 2- to 3-inch memory foam or latex topper adds the cushioning a side sleeper's shoulder and hip need, at a fraction of the cost of a new bed. A topper will not fix a mattress that sags or has a body impression, though.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
