          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Side sleeping comes down to one balance: enough give at the shoulder and hip, enough support at the waist. For most people that means a medium hybrid like the Helix Midnight Luxe. Lighter sleepers can go softer, heavier sleepers should go sturdier, and anyone who moves around a lot should favor a responsive hybrid over slow memory foam.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, use the trial. Give your body about a month to adjust, swap your pillow if your neck complains, and remember that a mattress makes sleep more comfortable but does not treat pain. If shoulder, hip or back pain persists, a doctor or physical therapist is the right next step, not another mattress.
